Subject: [PATCH] webrtc: offer only UDP families the proxy relay can carry

Behind a SOCKS5 proxy, WebRTC gathers UDP candidates only in the address
families the proxy host resolves to, and drops interfaces of other
families before any port exists. With UDP blocked, the port allocator
disables UDP and STUN the way Chrome's disable_non_proxied_udp policy
does. In both cases ICE gathering completes, so iceGatheringState
reaches complete and end-of-candidates fires. A port left gathering
forever is a state no stock Chrome configuration reaches.

--- a/net/socket/socks5_datagram_server_socket.h
+++ b/net/socket/socks5_datagram_server_socket.h
@@ -62,7 +62,11 @@
